    },
    {
      "text": "hyperparameters µ0 and τ0.",
      "bbox": [
        110.16093444824219,
        372.0419616699219,
        231.1625213623047,
        382.3827209472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Using eq. (34) as weights in eq. (24) gives the eﬀective sample size of importance sampling with",
      "bbox": [
        122.11591339111328,
        383.9969482421875,
        538.552490234375,
        392.8437194824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MCMC samples. The search for the lower bound in Step 3 will stop when the optimal prior is close",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609115600586,
        395.9519348144531,
        538.5925903320312,
        404.7987060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to the prior used in the MCMC (Figure 3). How close is determined by the assigned ESStarget in",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609115600586,
        407.90692138671875,
        538.565673828125,
        418.2486877441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 4, which in our example is set to 5 000 and 10 000 samples. The eﬀective sample size for the",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        419.8619079589844,
        538.5526733398438,
        428.70867919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MCMC samples in Step 2 is set to exceed ESStarget by at least 20%, i.e. MCMC sampling in Step",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        431.8179016113281,
        538.5830078125,
        442.1586608886719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2 will be run until an eﬀective sample size of 6 000 and 12 000 samples has been reached.",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        443.77288818359375,
        500.14691162109375,
        452.6196594238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimization in Step 3 is performed by simulated annealing, [10, 22], using the optim function",
      "bbox": [
        122.11592102050781,
        455.7278747558594,
        538.5758056640625,
        464.57464599609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "from the optimx package [31] in R.",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        467.682861328125,
        262.3464660644531,
        476.5296325683594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5.4. The lower bound of the expected overall eﬀect. We illustrate the method using two",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        487.10784912109375,
        538.573974609375,
        495.9546203613281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diﬀerent ESStarget and two choices of initial values (µ′",
      "bbox": [
        110.16091918945312,
        497.1305236816406,
        352.6612854003906,
        509.4035949707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0 = −7, τ ′",
      "bbox": [
        350.3669128417969,
        497.1305236816406,
        398.71728515625,
        510.3825988769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0 = 6) and (µ′",
      "bbox": [
        395.294921875,
        497.1305236816406,
        461.4252624511719,
        510.3825988769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0 = 10, τ ′",
      "bbox": [
        459.1308898925781,
        497.1305236816406,
        504.7132568359375,
        510.3825988769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0 = 10).",
      "bbox": [
        501.2918701171875,
        499.0628356933594,
        538.5656127929688,
        510.3825988769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The number of iterations of iterative importance sampling ranges between 2 and 3 with an eﬀective",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        511.0178527832031,
        538.5827026367188,
        519.8646240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sample size between 11 640 and 14 305, see (Table 1, 2 and 3). Note that the eﬀective samples size",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        522.9727783203125,
        538.5227661132812,
        531.819580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for the MCMC sample is derived based on the hyperparameters in the previous iteration.",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        534.9277954101562,
        500.04730224609375,
        543.7745971679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The estimated lower bound on the expected overall eﬀect over M is 12.1 µg/l (Table 1, 2 and",
      "bbox": [
        122.11589050292969,
        546.324951171875,
        538.568115234375,
        555.7296142578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3). We also run the method using diﬀerent random seeds which gives an estimated lower bound",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        558.8387451171875,
        538.592529296875,
        567.685546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on the expected overall eﬀect between 12.07 and 12.24 µg/l. The bound is lower than 19.9 which",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        570.7937622070312,
        538.587646484375,
        579.6405639648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is the estimated eﬀect in a standard Bayesian analysis using a ﬂat prior centered at zero (µ0 = 0",
      "bbox": [
        110.16085815429688,
        582.748779296875,
        538.560546875,
        593.089599609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and τ0 = 1 000). The lower bound is obtained at the corner of the prior region (i.e. µ0 = −8",
      "bbox": [
        110.16085815429688,
        594.1459350585938,
        538.5592041015625,
        605.0445556640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and τ0 = 5). The bound obtained by iterative importance sampling is compared to one estimated",
      "bbox": [
        110.16085815429688,
        606.6588134765625,
        538.596435546875,
        617.0006103515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by a grid search method across a regular grid of hyperparameters (which yields a total of 4 773",
      "bbox": [
        110.16085815429688,
        618.61376953125,
        538.6024169921875,
        627.4605712890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hyperparameter values). The grid search method gives a lower expected bound of 12.09 µg/l which",
      "bbox": [
        110.16085815429688,
        630.5697631835938,
        538.561279296875,
        639.4165649414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is close to the one found using iterative importance sampling. It takes much longer time to run a",
      "bbox": [
        110.160888671875,
        642.5247802734375,
        538.592529296875,
        651.37158203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
